{"text": "To target 24 using the numbers [5, 10, 13, 13] with each number used exactly once and the operations +, -, *, /, we can use the following expression:", "start": 0, "end": 149, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 - 5) × (13 - 10) = 24", "start": 151, "end": 176, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Breaking it down:", "start": 178, "end": 195, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1. Calculate 13 - 5:", "start": 197, "end": 217, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 5 = 8", "start": 219, "end": 229, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "2. Calculate 13 - 10:", "start": 231, "end": 252, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 10 = 3", "start": 254, "end": 265, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "3. Multiply the results from steps 1 and 2:", "start": 267, "end": 310, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "8 × 3 = 24", "start": 312, "end": 322, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Thus, the expression (13 - 5) × (13 - 10) equals 24.", "start": 324, "end": 376, "label": "inform"}
